## Evidence

The deterministic-validation specification documents the source-linked local
Jig checkout, ignored launchers/runtime, tracked `.jig/` authority, integration
refresh command, and canonical `jig validate --fail-fast --root .` invocation.

CI is explicitly deferred. The current local Jig workflow is the only canonical
validation surface; a future CI service is warranted only by a concrete public
contribution or release-automation need and must invoke the same tracked Jig
policy instead of defining independent gates.
